svg.desc:
Orbital periods are in true proportion (one Earth year = 12 s). Every orbit wheel meshes with a 12-tooth pinion;
tooth counts and speeds obey the gear law. Day lengths are compressed (one Earth day = 3 s) but keep their real ratios and directions
for Earth to Neptune; Mercury and Venus keep their real spin-to-orbit ratios. Sizes and distances are not to scale.
